  "applies_to": "Samsung MIM-B19N Modbus interface module on the R1/R2 bus of one outdoor system with up to 48 indoor units (installation manual DB68-07538A-00).",
  "summary": "The MIM-B19N links one Samsung outdoor system (up to 4 modular outdoor units) and up to 48 indoor units, hydro units, AHU kits, ERVs, chillers or FCUs on the R1/R2 bus to a Modbus RTU master. Each indoor unit gets a fixed 50-register block. This map covers the module status registers and the indoor-unit block: on/off, mode, fan speed, setpoints, room and water temperatures, errors, ventilation and hot-water functions. Addresses are given for indoor unit 0.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The table prints both a 1-based register number and the Modbus PDU address; the PDU address is used. Indoor unit n (0-47) occupies PDU addresses 50 + n*50 + k. This map lists indoor unit 0 (addresses 50-81); add 50 per unit, e.g. indoor unit 3 on/off = 50 + 150 + 2 = 202."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus Interface Module MIM-B19N Installation Manual",
    "doc_number": "DB68-07538A-00",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://midsummerwholesale.co.uk/pdfs/mim-b19n-manual.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "specifications and communication settings p. 8; communication sequence p. 9; address switches pp. 11-12; register table pp. 13-16"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Source host: the unaltered Samsung manual hosted by a UK distributor; we did not find a public Samsung copy.",
    "All values are single 16-bit registers, big-endian. Temperatures are Celsius x10; the manual's ranges go down to -41 °C, so they are listed as signed.",
    "The manual marks each point R, W or R/W per unit type (indoor, HE/HT/EHS, AHU kit, ERV, ERV+, chiller, FCU, FCU kit). Read-only points are listed as input registers (FC 04) and writable points as holding registers (FC 03/06/16); the module supports both read functions but the manual does not say which table each read-only point lives in, so try FC 03 if FC 04 is refused.",
    "Access shown is the widest across unit types; a point marked '-' for a unit type does not apply to it (e.g. water temperatures only for HE/HT/EHS and chillers, ventilation only for ERV).",
    "Left out: the MCC chiller error-information registers (+26/+27, packed bytes) and the reserved ranges.",
    "Any write to a holding register is always forwarded to the indoor unit as a command, even if the value is unchanged."
  ],
